@startuml
allowmixing
title 5G Traffic Steering with NGFW/SASE (Clean Layout)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam roundcorner 15
skinparam padding 8
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 45
left to right direction

' -----------------------------
' UE + RAN
' -----------------------------
rectangle "UE + NG-RAN" as RAN {
  component "UE" as UE
  component "gNB\n(5G Base Station)" as GNB
}

' -----------------------------
' 5GC Control Plane
' -----------------------------
rectangle "5G Core (5GC)\nControl Plane" as CP {
  together {
    component "PCF\n(Policy)" as PCF
    component "SMF\n(Session Mgmt)" as SMF
  }
}

' -----------------------------
' 5GC User Plane
' -----------------------------
rectangle "5G Core (5GC)\nUser Plane" as UP {
  component "UPF\n(User Plane Function)" as UPF
}

' -----------------------------
' Security chain + DN
' -----------------------------
rectangle "Security Service Chain" as SEC {
  component "NGFW / SASE" as NGFW
}

cloud "Data Network (DN)\nInternet / Enterprise" as DN

' -----------------------------
' Alignment helpers (hidden)
' -----------------------------
PCF -[hidden]-> SMF
SMF -[hidden]-> UPF
GNB -[hidden]-> UPF
NGFW -[hidden]-> DN

' -----------------------------
' Traffic + Interfaces
' -----------------------------
UE --> GNB : 5G NR Air\n(User traffic)

GNB --> UPF : N3 (GTP-U)\nUser plane packets

PCF --> SMF : Npcf\nQoS + Steering intent

SMF --> UPF : N4 (PFCP)\nInstall PDR/FAR/QER/URR rules

UPF --> NGFW : N6 Steering\n(redirect / service-chain)
NGFW --> DN : Forward clean traffic

UPF ..> DN : N6 Direct\n(Bypass path)\n(optional)

' -----------------------------
' Notes: move details here
' -----------------------------
note right of UPF
UPF executes:
- PDR: match traffic
- FAR: action (forward/redirect/drop)
- QER: QoS enforce
- URR: usage report
end note

note right of PCF
Policy examples:
- enterprise slice => inspect
- unknown domain => inspect
- trusted apps => bypass
end note

note bottom
Goal:
- Keep heavy text out of components
- Use notes for clarity
- Avoid arrow label collisions
end note
@enduml